---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { LANGS, type Lang, t } from "../../data/site";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return LANGS.map((lang) => ({ params: { lang } }));
}
const lang = Astro.params.lang as Lang;
---

<Base lang={lang} title={t("about", lang)} path="about/">
  <article class="narrow">
    {
      lang === "en" ? (
        <>
          <h1>About</h1>
          <p class="lead">Every child deserves to understand why maths works — not only the children whose parents can pay for a good tutor.</p>
          <p>
            Boxi Math makes short videos that each answer one “why”: why 8 + 5 is easier if you split the 5, why 1/2 and 2/4 are the
            same point, why a negative times a negative is positive. Each one is drawn so you can see the idea, names the common
            mix-up it fixes, and shows where the picture stops working.
          </p>
          <h2>How it is organised</h2>
          <p>
            By <strong>stage</strong>, not by school year. Children move on when an idea makes sense, and school years differ from
            country to country anyway, so every video lists the matching year in China, the US, the UK and Singapore. Under the
            stages are six <strong>seeds</strong> — habits of mind worth planting early, like “the equals sign is a balance” and
            “mistakes are fine, try it”.
          </p>
          <h2>Open</h2>
          <p>
            Videos and text are CC BY 4.0: use them in class, translate them, remix them — just credit Boxi Yu. The animation tools
            behind them are open source too, at <a href="https://github.com/animind-ai">animind-ai</a>.
          </p>
          <h2>Who</h2>
          <p>
            Made by <a href="https://boxiyu.github.io">Boxi Yu</a>, a researcher in AI and software engineering who wants good
            maths teaching to cost nothing.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <h1>关于</h1>
          <p class="lead">每个孩子都应该懂得数学为什么成立，不只是请得起好家教的孩子。</p>
          <p>
            Boxi Math 做短视频，每集只回答一个「为什么」：为什么 8+5 先拆 5，为什么 1/2 和 2/4 是同一个点，为什么负负得正。
            每集都把道理画出来，点出它要纠正的常见误会，也讲清楚这张图什么时候不灵。
          </p>
          <h2>怎么组织</h2>
          <p>
            按<strong>阶段</strong>，不按年级。孩子懂了再往前；各国年级本来也不一样，所以每集都标出中国、美国、英国、新加坡对应的年级。
            阶段之下还有六颗<strong>种子</strong>：越早种下越好的思维习惯，比如「等号是天平」「错了没关系，试试看」。
          </p>
          <h2>开放</h2>
          <p>
            视频和文字用 CC BY 4.0 授权：可以拿去上课、翻译、改编，注明作者 Boxi Yu 即可。做动画的工具也开源在{" "}
            <a href="https://github.com/animind-ai">animind-ai</a>。
          </p>
          <h2>作者</h2>
          <p>
            <a href="https://boxiyu.github.io">Boxi Yu</a>，做 AI 与软件工程研究，希望好的数学教育不花钱。
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }
  </article>
</Base>
